# SynAck SMS — Privacy and Security Notes

SynAck SMS is an Android SMS/MMS application based on the open-source QUIK/QKSMS project.

## What the app handles
- SMS and MMS message content, phone numbers, contact information, and attachments as needed to provide the messaging features.
- Messages are exchanged through the cellular carrier's normal SMS/MMS infrastructure. **End-to-end encrypted SynAck Secure Chat is planned, not yet implemented.** Normal SMS/MMS content is not protected from the carrier by this app.
- Messages may be stored in Android's system SMS/MMS provider and an app-local Realm database.

## Network and third parties
- Optional third-party Call Control and Should I Answer integrations were removed.
- MMS handling may involve connections to carrier-operated servers. Opening external links, support pages, or contact actions uses Android's normal system intents.
- The on-device app does not download Google Messages to update carrier configurations. The one-time GitHub Actions import is developer-operated and manual-only.

## Local diagnostic data
- Optional diagnostic logging can create files in Downloads when enabled. Logs might contain sensitive diagnostic information.
- SMS backup files are exported as plaintext JSON to a user-chosen storage location; treat them as sensitive and protect them accordingly.
- Android-level data and notification permissions are required to operate as the default SMS app.

## Status
This project is under development. A repository static inventory and partial manual code review have been performed, **not** a complete dependency, APK or runtime security audit. Do not assume encrypted chats or guaranteed absence of external data transfers based on the current review.

